sketchBlocks.bodyMarkdown:
Express middleware runs in registration order. A middleware function receives `req`, `res`, and `next`.

```js
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  console.log(`${req.method} ${req.path}`);
  next();
});

app.get("/api/events", (req, res) => {
  res.status(200).json(events);
});
```

**Line by line:** `app.use(...)` registers middleware for incoming requests. The middleware reads request metadata and logs it. Calling `next()` passes control to the next matching middleware or route. The GET handler then builds the response.

If middleware neither sends a response nor calls `next()`, the request can stop before it reaches the route. That makes request flow and ordering part of the API design.

