sketchBlocks.bodyMarkdown:
Built-in middleware can prepare the request for later routes. `express.json()` parses a JSON request body when a request actually has one.

```js
app.use(express.json());

app.use((req, res, next) => {
  req.apiName = "campus-api";
  next();
});

app.get("/api/about", (req, res) => {
  res.status(200).json({ api: req.apiName });
});
```

**Step by step:** JSON parsing is registered first. The next middleware adds shared request context and calls `next()`. The route runs afterward and can read that context. Registration order therefore describes the path a request follows.

The current module remains read-only; JSON body parsing is introduced here so the middleware model is clear before Module 3 adds write routes that consume request bodies.

